WEBVTT

00:01.180 --> 00:06.020
Dear Mother, right now I'm separated from the Dandelion Troupe and am traveling alone.

00:06.780 --> 00:12.860
All of my money was stolen from me and I had some scary encounters, but I managed to cross the English Channel and have entered England.

00:13.700 --> 00:16.960
Soon I will reach Applefield Orphanage, where I was raised.

00:26.750 --> 00:27.910
NAAJA

00:26.750 --> 00:27.910
Nadja

00:27.940 --> 00:30.410
kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:27.960 --> 00:30.410
With your eyes

00:30.410 --> 00:31.570
NAAJA

00:30.460 --> 00:31.570
Nadja

00:31.590 --> 00:33.840
nani ga mieru

00:31.590 --> 00:33.840
What do you see?

00:34.060 --> 00:36.950
haruka tooku hikaru

00:34.060 --> 00:36.950
Shining in the far distance,

00:37.100 --> 00:39.240
mirai no tobira

00:37.100 --> 00:39.240
The door to the future,

00:40.380 --> 00:43.790
sagashiteiru

00:40.380 --> 00:43.790
That's what I'm searching for

00:43.790 --> 00:51.000
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:51.710 --> 00:55.120
minna egao de aetara

00:51.710 --> 00:55.120
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:55.220 --> 00:58.480
arasoimo kitto nakunaru

00:55.220 --> 00:58.480
I'm sure there would be no more fighting

00:58.550 --> 01:01.930
kon nani mo tanoshiku naru

00:58.580 --> 01:01.930
It could be so much more fun

01:01.960 --> 01:05.410
sekai wa hiruikedo hitotsune

01:01.960 --> 01:05.410
The world is wide, but it's still one

01:05.780 --> 01:09.140
tabi no owari wa mienai

01:05.780 --> 01:09.140
I can't see the end of the journey

01:09.170 --> 01:12.330
kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:09.170 --> 01:12.330
God is the only one who can possibly know

01:12.500 --> 01:16.150
itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:12.500 --> 01:16.150
To the people who, someday, I will meet again

01:16.150 --> 01:18.300
te wo furinagara

01:16.150 --> 01:18.300
I will go waving

01:18.450 --> 01:25.190
toki ni wa BURUU ni naru himo aru kedo

01:18.450 --> 01:25.190
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:25.190 --> 01:27.930
ushiro mukanai

01:25.190 --> 01:27.930
But I won't look back

01:28.200 --> 01:33.240
yume ga kanau hima de

01:28.200 --> 01:33.240
Until the day my dream comes true

01:33.410 --> 01:36.790
NAAJA kimi no hoho emi wa

01:33.410 --> 01:36.790
Nadja, your smile

01:36.870 --> 01:40.070
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:36.870 --> 01:40.070
Nadja, you give me courage

02:10.900 --> 02:12.620
Be careful, young lady.

02:13.090 --> 02:15.640
I will! Thank you so much, mister.

02:19.960 --> 02:23.360
Surely the chairwoman will testify that I'm the real Nadja.

02:23.810 --> 02:25.540
Then I'll be able to meet my mother.

02:26.500 --> 02:28.100
Well, let's go to the orphanage!

02:29.410 --> 02:31.310
I'll be able to see the director and everyone else.

02:31.910 --> 02:33.310
I wonder if they're all doing well?

02:41.930 --> 02:46.790
Alone at Home

02:47.270 --> 02:49.760
Vienna

02:47.340 --> 02:49.180
You're doing so well right now, Nadja.

02:50.110 --> 02:51.690
You're a quick learner.

02:52.280 --> 02:55.490
It's because you're a good teacher, Aunt Hilda.

02:56.700 --> 02:57.490
Nadja.

02:59.240 --> 03:00.030
Mother!

03:03.200 --> 03:04.450
My, how splendid!

03:05.000 --> 03:06.870
Is all of this for you and her?

03:07.290 --> 03:07.870
Yes...

03:08.250 --> 03:12.880
I didn't know what sort of sweets Nadja would like, so I got a little carried away.

03:16.630 --> 03:17.340
Nadja...

03:17.760 --> 03:18.640
I'm sorry.

03:19.050 --> 03:25.640
Even though I'm happy just to know my mother is alive... to receive such kindness is like a dream.

03:26.310 --> 03:27.440
Nadja.

03:41.280 --> 03:43.530
It was painful at the orphanage.

03:44.200 --> 03:48.500
I was always hungry and the scary teachers hit me a lot...

03:49.920 --> 03:51.080
That's terrible...

03:52.040 --> 03:53.500
It's alright now, Nadja.

03:54.380 --> 03:56.510
I will stay by your side from now on.

03:56.710 --> 04:02.550
You may not have known me as a mother, but let's take our time to become mother and daughter.

04:03.140 --> 04:03.810
I will!

04:04.600 --> 04:05.470
This is good.

04:05.810 --> 04:09.020
She's really made them believe that she is Nadja.

04:09.850 --> 04:12.310
She's quite the actress.

04:15.110 --> 04:16.650
I'll go get more tea.

04:17.320 --> 04:19.110
I will do it, aunt.

04:19.400 --> 04:24.530
It's alright. You haven't gotten the chance to speak with your mother since you met her.

04:24.910 --> 04:25.790
I would like to do it.

04:26.290 --> 04:29.210
I would like the opportunity to serve my mother tea.

04:36.550 --> 04:38.460
I'm sorry, Hilda.

04:39.090 --> 04:42.930
I should be the one to educate her and raise her.

04:43.550 --> 04:47.310
But father said I would be too soft on her, so he didn't allow it.

04:47.850 --> 04:49.310
That's very much like the Duke.

04:49.850 --> 04:53.690
He's very strict when it comes to etiquette and manners in this house.

04:54.360 --> 04:56.270
Yes, he's very stubborn.

04:56.690 --> 04:58.990
Nadja isn't a burden on you, is she?

04:59.400 --> 05:03.870
Not at all. She enjoys being taught. She is also intelligent and well-mannered.

05:04.320 --> 05:07.620
She will surely become a woman befitting the Preminger House.

05:08.490 --> 05:14.420
My father may think about whether she befits the House or not, but it doesn't matter to me.

05:15.000 --> 05:15.420
Huh?

05:16.380 --> 05:19.920
I only care that she is alive and well...

05:32.330 --> 05:35.610
I wasn't the one running around Applefield.

05:35.930 --> 05:37.610
This is the real me.

05:38.300 --> 05:39.880
I'm a princess, you know?

05:40.150 --> 05:40.770
Nadja!

05:41.710 --> 05:42.550
Come here.

05:44.320 --> 05:46.520
What are you doing? Hurry and come.

05:49.760 --> 05:51.530
When you are called, you have to come at once.

05:52.200 --> 05:54.500
I am not one to receive orders from you.

05:54.790 --> 05:56.790
Please don't boss me around like you are all high and mighty.

05:56.890 --> 05:57.750
What did you say?

05:58.050 --> 06:00.030
Who do you think you're talking to in such a way!

06:00.200 --> 06:01.460
I am Nadja.

06:01.830 --> 06:06.050
Since I am Duke Preminger's granddaughter, it is my right to become heiress to this House.

06:06.570 --> 06:09.090
I am different from someone like you, who has been disinherited.

06:10.740 --> 06:12.320
So, what matter did you wish to discuss?

06:12.760 --> 06:14.740
No, it doesn't matter...

06:14.940 --> 06:16.220
I am busy.

06:16.590 --> 06:18.340
If there is nothing to discuss, please don't call me.

06:18.790 --> 06:19.920
Since I'm in a hurry...

06:20.520 --> 06:21.130
Excuse me.

06:27.280 --> 06:29.130
Such an impudent little girl.

06:29.650 --> 06:30.690
Well, it doesn't matter.

06:31.330 --> 06:35.530
Do your utmost and become heiress of the Preminger House.

06:35.970 --> 06:37.820
In the end, you are an impostor.

06:38.190 --> 06:42.410
Such a weak girl can't do me any harm.

06:43.150 --> 06:49.620
If she becomes a bird in a gilded cage, I can utilize the assets of the Preminger House as I wish.

06:54.980 --> 07:01.770
I have witnessed that Nadja is training to be a noble lady with Hilda everyday with zeal.

07:02.410 --> 07:03.350
Is that so.

07:11.000 --> 07:11.670
What is it?

07:12.260 --> 07:13.840
Are you not happy?

07:14.330 --> 07:17.520
You have found the successor you were searching for.

07:18.780 --> 07:22.140
It hasn't been decided that Nadja will become my successor.

07:22.930 --> 07:24.980
Even if she has the blood of the Dukedom...

07:25.170 --> 07:27.000
...useless people are still useless.

07:27.370 --> 07:29.070
Herman is a good example.

07:29.960 --> 07:35.590
I have to ascertain whether Nadja is fit to inherit the Preminger House.

07:41.100 --> 07:43.890
I came without notice, so everyone should be surprised.

07:44.280 --> 07:45.890
Ah, I want to hurry and see them!

07:51.240 --> 07:51.810
Almost there.

07:52.550 --> 07:53.540
Almost there.

07:57.020 --> 07:57.760
Almost there.

08:02.030 --> 08:04.480
Miss Chairwoman! Everyone!

08:35.260 --> 08:38.540
This...is Applefield Orphanage, isn't it?

08:52.470 --> 08:53.730
What is this?

08:54.150 --> 08:55.800
Everyone...where are you?

08:59.920 --> 09:00.760
Bibi!

09:01.310 --> 09:02.170
Daisy!

09:02.660 --> 09:03.600
Are you here?

09:04.020 --> 09:04.810
Alex!

09:05.350 --> 09:06.000
Nicole!

09:06.220 --> 09:07.060
Peter!

09:13.060 --> 09:13.750
Who's there?

09:29.380 --> 09:30.960
Everyone, where are you?

09:31.350 --> 09:33.870
Miss Chairwoman! Miss Eda!

09:43.130 --> 09:44.110
These are...

09:45.940 --> 09:48.140
The letters I wrote the chairwoman...

09:48.880 --> 09:49.640
This too...

09:49.960 --> 09:50.680
And this too.

09:51.890 --> 09:52.680
Why...

10:04.700 --> 10:06.060
Um, excuse me.

10:06.800 --> 10:09.890
I want to ask you about Applefield Orphanage.

10:10.310 --> 10:11.840
Applefield?

10:12.580 --> 10:13.740
The one up on the hill?

10:14.260 --> 10:16.480
Yes. It seems strange.

10:16.870 --> 10:18.060
No one is there.

10:18.180 --> 10:19.390
And then...

10:19.840 --> 10:23.640
You...those clothes...were you a child there?

10:24.010 --> 10:24.500
Yes.

10:24.920 --> 10:25.860
I see.

10:26.450 --> 10:28.630
I guess no one's told you.

10:28.820 --> 10:33.290
Nobody lives there anymore. The orphanage has been abandoned.

10:34.580 --> 10:38.990
The children have been placed at other orphanages.

10:39.190 --> 10:42.350
That can't be... What about the chairwoman?

10:43.830 --> 10:47.040
The chairwoman you speak of has died.

11:10.570 --> 11:12.720
The chairwoman has died?

11:12.870 --> 11:13.470
Yes.

11:14.130 --> 11:18.230
Then the funds for the orphanage ran out and it eventually closed.

11:19.070 --> 11:19.520
This can't be...

11:20.310 --> 11:20.800
This can't be!

11:21.340 --> 11:23.020
How could the chairwoman be dead.

11:23.790 --> 11:25.760
She was so healthy.

11:25.910 --> 11:27.120
There was an accident.

11:44.550 --> 11:49.120
To save the child from the falling wooden boards, she...

11:50.840 --> 11:55.340
Everyone in town thought it was a pity to lose such a valuable person.

11:56.350 --> 11:56.990
It's a lie.

11:57.930 --> 11:59.210
I can understand your feelings, but...

11:59.680 --> 12:02.450
I can't believe such a thing. Absolutely not!

12:05.060 --> 12:05.830
Come with me.

12:09.430 --> 12:10.350
What is this?

12:10.990 --> 12:13.090
The Chairwoman's grave.

12:15.060 --> 12:19.410
Here rests the beloved mother of Applefield.

12:24.050 --> 12:24.760
Are you alright?

12:25.580 --> 12:26.250
Young miss?

12:35.330 --> 12:36.340
Nadja

12:38.170 --> 12:39.110
Nadja

12:40.540 --> 12:41.350
Nadja!

12:42.980 --> 12:43.900
Nadja.

12:45.800 --> 12:47.160
Miss Chairwoman...

12:48.190 --> 12:49.160
Miss Chairwoman!

13:01.890 --> 13:05.030
Fr...om...Ri...ta...

13:07.750 --> 13:08.460
Abel...

13:08.730 --> 13:10.290
There is one plate too many.

13:10.560 --> 13:12.860
Ah, sorry. I forgot.

13:13.620 --> 13:14.860
Thomas!

13:15.320 --> 13:17.350
Take me to a post office.

13:17.520 --> 13:19.000
A post office? Why?

13:19.270 --> 13:20.780
I want to send Nadja a letter.

13:21.270 --> 13:24.930
Rita, we don't know where Nadja is right now.

13:25.250 --> 13:26.260
It will be alright.

13:26.510 --> 13:33.450
Look, I've written "To Nadja" on it. If we give this to the postman, he will deliver it to her.

13:34.110 --> 13:34.850
Rita...

13:37.670 --> 13:39.200
Sylvie, what's wrong?

13:39.300 --> 13:41.540
It can't be delivered like that...

13:42.040 --> 13:42.580
It will!

13:43.690 --> 13:47.910
She wrote this with all her might for Nadja. How can it not be delivered?

13:48.970 --> 13:49.860
Kennosuke...

13:50.480 --> 13:53.050
Rita, I will take you to the post office.

13:53.420 --> 13:53.910
Let's go!

14:00.500 --> 14:03.020
I wonder where Nadja is right now.

14:03.560 --> 14:05.340
I hope she is well, but...

14:12.500 --> 14:14.400
Ah, watch out.

14:17.290 --> 14:18.180
Huh?

14:19.390 --> 14:20.450
Miss Chairwoman...

14:21.410 --> 14:22.970
Why did you die?

14:24.970 --> 14:25.660
Why...

14:27.360 --> 14:28.180
Why!?

14:38.100 --> 14:40.420
Hey, hey, put on your clothes properly.

14:40.790 --> 14:42.400
Wash your faces properly.

14:45.240 --> 14:47.140
Nadja, I'm counting on you to watch after them.

15:22.490 --> 15:26.490
Now there's no one that can testify that I am Nadja.

15:26.960 --> 15:29.350
I can't meet my mother anymore.

15:54.290 --> 15:55.300
Everyone...

15:55.890 --> 15:57.300
Why are they all laughing?

15:57.620 --> 15:58.930
How can they all laugh?

16:03.200 --> 16:03.870
Mother!

16:08.140 --> 16:09.870
Mother! Mother!

16:12.610 --> 16:14.190
Wait, Mother!

16:14.630 --> 16:16.430
I am Nadja!

16:17.120 --> 16:18.180
Wait!

16:18.600 --> 16:19.320
Mother!

16:20.180 --> 16:22.090
I am Nadja!

16:22.730 --> 16:23.910
Mother!

16:36.630 --> 16:38.400
Mother...why can't I....

16:39.190 --> 16:41.190
...meet you anymore?

16:51.780 --> 16:52.400
Raphael!

16:53.190 --> 16:54.800
It's been a while, Nadja.

16:55.640 --> 16:56.350
Raphael.

16:57.190 --> 16:58.350
Raphael!

17:11.880 --> 17:12.550
Here.

17:14.650 --> 17:15.810
You must be hungry.

17:16.200 --> 17:18.350
If you don't eat properly, you won't have any energy.

17:41.630 --> 17:45.680
Raphael... I don't know what to do.

17:48.390 --> 17:50.690
I don't think I can see my mother anymore.

17:51.400 --> 17:54.100
They won't believe that I'm Nadja.

17:54.980 --> 17:56.270
Even though I finally found her.

17:56.640 --> 17:57.580
Isn't that great?

17:59.550 --> 18:02.590
I heard it from Sylvie the first time I met you in Paris.

18:03.400 --> 18:05.300
That you were traveling to find your mother.

18:06.320 --> 18:11.940
Even though you didn't know her face, her name, nor whether she was alive or not.

18:13.820 --> 18:14.910
You found her, didn't you?

18:18.360 --> 18:19.230
That's wonderful, isn't it?

18:20.170 --> 18:20.980
Thank you.

18:24.980 --> 18:27.330
I can see wings on your shoulders.

18:29.450 --> 18:31.050
All humans have wings.

18:31.970 --> 18:34.580
Your wings won't lose to anything.

18:35.030 --> 18:37.740
They are heading towards tomorrow, working hard, and carrying hope.

18:38.090 --> 18:39.970
Wings...with hope?

18:42.530 --> 18:44.460
Right now I don't have any hope...

18:45.590 --> 18:48.630
Right now you are tired so your wings are resting.

18:50.090 --> 18:52.480
Your are a person who will never lose her hope.

18:59.320 --> 19:00.650
Something like hope...

19:01.270 --> 19:04.280
Even though I've lost the chance of seeing my mother.

19:06.010 --> 19:08.780
But...I have learned that she is still alive.

19:09.940 --> 19:12.530
Her name is Collette. I even saw her face.

19:14.110 --> 19:17.490
I didn't know anything when I left the orphanage.

19:18.080 --> 19:20.700
I learned so many things as I was traveling.

19:30.850 --> 19:31.710
That's it.

19:32.030 --> 19:33.390
This is the starting point.

19:34.750 --> 19:41.020
This is where I celebrated my 13th birthday and received my mother's trunk with her dress and diary.

19:41.930 --> 19:44.990
You have already been taking care of the brooch.

19:46.000 --> 19:48.670
And now you have received her dress and diary.

19:49.880 --> 19:53.410
They are all important things linking you to your mother.

19:56.970 --> 19:58.270
It's wonderful, isn't it?

19:58.820 --> 20:00.890
If you could meet your mother sometime.

20:04.170 --> 20:07.930
Nadja, this just arrived for you.

20:09.260 --> 20:10.120
That's right!

20:10.350 --> 20:14.890
I don't know who sent the package, but I do know it was dispatched from London.

20:15.850 --> 20:17.850
Raphael, I remembered!

20:18.320 --> 20:19.090
You know...

20:20.000 --> 20:20.960
Your wings are flapping.

20:22.690 --> 20:29.700
Nadja, your wings—like your heart—are strong, unhurt, and also beautiful.

21:00.980 --> 21:01.700
Raphael?

21:03.470 --> 21:04.190
Raphael!

21:14.680 --> 21:15.450
Raphael...

21:16.580 --> 21:17.450
Thank you.

21:18.190 --> 21:18.900
Time to eat!

21:30.580 --> 21:33.440
Miss Chairwoman, I won't give up.

21:34.090 --> 21:35.810
Surely, I will meet my mother.

21:36.330 --> 21:38.130
Please watch over me from Heaven.

21:42.550 --> 21:45.120
A new path will surely open if I go to London.

21:45.760 --> 21:46.800
It will work out somehow.

21:47.320 --> 21:48.730
Let's go, to London!

22:14.680 --> 22:17.940
RONDON donyori haretara PARI

22:14.680 --> 22:17.940
Paris is sunnier than London

22:18.110 --> 22:21.130
KARUMEN menyori PAERIYA suki

22:18.110 --> 22:21.130
Carmen likes paella more than pasta

22:21.570 --> 22:27.770
SUPEEDO no jyoou kimagure yasan

22:21.570 --> 22:27.770
The Queen of Spades is a fickle person

22:28.680 --> 22:29.940
kitto

22:28.680 --> 22:29.940
Indeed

22:32.700 --> 22:35.170
nayan datte muda yo

22:32.700 --> 22:35.170
It's no use worrying about it

22:35.220 --> 22:38.830
kesera sera sera sera

22:35.220 --> 22:38.830
Que sera sera, sera sera

22:39.070 --> 22:43.760
ashita nante itsumo naru youni

22:39.070 --> 22:43.760
Tomorrow's going to be whatever it was meant

22:43.860 --> 22:45.220
naru naru

22:43.860 --> 22:45.220
To be, to be

22:45.620 --> 22:50.550
sekai kaeru tobi KONKUURU

22:45.620 --> 22:50.550
The tree frog won.

22:51.050 --> 22:55.000
yuushou shita yo amagaeru

22:51.050 --> 22:55.000
The world frog jumping contest

22:58.180 --> 23:04.330
koneko chan no ashi no urawa

22:58.180 --> 23:04.330
Under the kitten's paw

23:04.800 --> 23:10.920
otentou sama no nioi da ne

23:04.800 --> 23:10.920
Is the scent of the sun, right?

23:13.780 --> 23:17.140
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

23:13.780 --> 23:17.140
Paris is sunnier than London

23:17.190 --> 23:20.150
KARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

23:17.190 --> 23:20.150
Carmen likes paella more than pasta

23:20.700 --> 23:27.120
michikusa shite iru baaijyanai ne

23:20.700 --> 23:27.120
It's not the time to hang around

23:27.960 --> 23:32.470
kitto kitto

23:27.960 --> 23:32.470
Indeed, indeed

23:40.590 --> 23:41.960
Tomorrow's Nadja

23:42.030 --> 23:45.560
There isn't anyone who can testify that I am Nadja.

23:46.450 --> 23:50.300
I, running into the city, walking alone with no clues...

23:50.870 --> 23:56.250
A certain pianist from a concert walks before my eyes.

23:57.120 --> 23:57.740
Hey, John.

23:58.010 --> 24:01.270
That song you are playing right now. I know it from my childhood.

24:02.480 --> 24:03.390
That piece is...

24:04.150 --> 24:04.990
Tomorrow's Nadja.

24:04.820 --> 24:06.820
The Lullaby That Piano is Connected To

24:06.370 --> 24:08.100
Now, the door to destiny opens.
